## Summary

Shipped a production-polished, Apple-idiomatic **`TirePressureSection`** SwiftUI surface (9 files, 2043 lines) at parity with `web/.../drive-detail/TirePressureSection.tsx`, committed as `7c851ba22`.

**What was built** (`apps/apple/TeslaSync/feature-views/TirePressureSection.*`):
- **Adapter/Projector** — Foundation-only port of the web `chartData`/`stats` derivation: SI(kPa)→display conversion (`convertPressureFromSI` 1:1 — kPa/psi/bar), per-wheel min/max over `value != null && > 0`, the line-presence-vs-range distinction, content gate = `stats.hasTirePressure`.
- **Model** — P1/S8 source seam + P1/S11 `view.opened` telemetry + P1/S10 i18n facade + `@Observable` state holder (phase, freshness, stale auto-refresh, offline cache).
- **Chart** — Swift Charts 4-series `LineMark` with **exact-hex** design tokens (FL #3b82f6→Speed, FR #10b981→Battery, RL #f59e0b→Energy, RR #ef4444→Temperature) + selection tooltip.
- **Views/Surface/Previews/strings/Tests** — all states render (loading/empty/error/stale/offline/content), 4 always-shown min/max tiles, legend, VoiceOver summaries, 7 source i18n keys, and 33 unit tests.

**Key correctness fix:** namespaced every symbol `TirePressureSection*` to avoid colliding with the pre-existing dashboard tire widgets (`TirePressureProjection`/`TirePressureUnit`/…); a 41-symbol sweep confirms zero new redeclarations.

**Gates (all green):** swiftformat `--lint` 0/8 · swiftlint `--strict` 0 violations · placeholder 0 · `swiftc -typecheck` iOS-18 + macOS-15 (Swift 6 strict concurrency) · **33/33 XCTest** (isolated SwiftPM) · xcodegen enumerates 9 files.

**Deferred (honest):** the full-app `xcodebuild build test` is recorded **macOS-pending** — blocked by pre-existing, unrelated repo state (unstaged `Shared.xcframework`, `DashboardWidgetSize` redefined ×15, 262 co-located `*.Tests.swift` in the app target, no signing identity), none originating in this surface. This matches the established precedent (ToolCard/AlertMessageEditor/FSMTimelineChart). Log ends `EXIT=0 / STATUS=DONE`.

